{
  "name": "unitype",
  "doc": "The system, described in its own terms.\n\nEvery type, declaration, and universe here serializes to plain JSON, which means each of them is also a value \u2014 and a value can be validated, moved between universes, generated as code, and passed to a proposition like any other. So describing the representation in the representation is not a trick: it is what makes a type an ordinary thing to compute with.\n\nKept honest by a test. The real declarations are serialized and checked against these, so this cannot quietly drift away from what it claims to describe.",
